/* /vibe-coding moved to /builds.

   Vibe Coding is no longer a content pillar. It is a TOPIC inside Learn and a
   SERIES (/series/vibe-coding, untouched) — a way of working, not a category of
   thing Adel makes. Builds is the pillar, and it is wider than coding: a build
   may be design, automation, prompting, hardware or a business, or several at
   once. See PUBLISHING.md.

   This redirect exists because /vibe-coding was a live, linkable URL. The build
   STORIES never needed one: zero builds were published under the old path, so
   the rename cost exactly this file and its Arabic twin.

   Same mechanism as /playground/passport — a prerendered redirect emits an HTML
   stub carrying a canonical and `noindex`, so the link keeps working and the
   index learns the new address. */
return Astro.redirect('/builds/', 301);
